'''Velken Tezeri''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] guard and [[arms dealer]]<ref name="AEYNTK">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> who worked for the [[Hutt]] [[crime lord]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]].

==Biography==
Velken Tezeri was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] who worked as an [[arms dealer]] before deciding to stabilize his situation by becoming a [[Security guard|guard]] for the [[Hutt]] [[crime lord]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]] at his [[Boba Fett's Palace|palace]] on the [[desert]] [[planet]] [[Tatooine]].<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> In [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Death" /> he was one of five guards chosen<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> to ride on board a [[Bantha-II cargo skiff]] carrying the [[prisoner]]s [[Luke Skywalker]], [[Han Solo]], and [[Chewbacca]] to the [[Great Pit of Carkoon]], where Jabba planned to [[Death|execute]] the trio by feeding them to a [[sarlacc]].<ref name="ROTJ" />

However, during the execution attempt, thanks to [[R2-D2]], Skywalker managed to break free and attacked the guards on his skiff. Tezeri tried to help his comrades to defeat Skywalker, so he took out his gun from his pocket, but Skywalker passed his [[lightsaber]] very close to him, causing Tezeri to slip and fall through a skiff's rail. With such bad luck, Tezeri fell to the sand and rolled until falling into the mouth of the Sarlacc, to slowly be digested over thousands of years.<ref name="ROTJ" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Velken Tezeri was played by stuntman [[Larry Holt]]<ref name="Actor">{{Blogspot|subdomain=starwarsaficionado|url=2014/09/behind-scenes-just-another-day-at-skiff.html|name=STAR WARS AFICIONADO WEBSITE|text=Behind the Scenes: Just Another Day at the Skiff!}}</ref> in the [[1983]] [[original trilogy]], film [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']].<ref name="ROTJ" /> In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], the character was first identified in the [[2015]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''.<ref name="AEYNTK" /> ''[[The Battle of Hoth and the Second Death Star]]'', an issue of [[De Agostini]]'s [[Star Wars Encyclopedia (series)|''Star Wars Encyclopedia'']] series<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> released on [[December 11]], [[2020]],<ref name="Altaya">{{Altaya|lang=fr|url=livres-bd/encyclopedie-star-wars|text=Official Star Wars Encyclopedia}}</ref> erroneously describes Tezeri as being on the second skiff rather than the one carrying the prisoners.<ref name="Encyclopedia" />

